title: Return anonymous listed-room rosters as alias#room@relay without machine metadata
---
B111 found that anonymous GET /list_rooms exposes raw member aliases for public and gated rooms. Preserve the roster feature, but expose presentation-only room recipient addresses in canonical alias#room@relay form. Do not expose machine ID, opaque_host_id, node_id, session_id, identity key, or any lease-routing metadata.

Acceptance criteria:
- Every members entry in an anonymous /list_rooms response is alias#room@relay, with the actual listed room ID. Bare aliases are absent.
- Public and gated rooms retain listability; unlisted/private remain omitted.
- Format only at the relay directory boundary in both InMemoryRelay and SqliteRelay; keep raw stored aliases for membership checks and room delivery.
- Do not look up leases to decorate roster addresses.
- A registered member with opaque_host_id/node_id/session_id causes none of those values to appear in directory JSON.
- Both backend implementations and HTTP tests assert identical response shapes; existing room-recipient parsing continues to accept the addresses.

Source seams: relay_backend_contract list_rooms, relay.ml InMemoryRelay/SqliteRelay/handle_list_rooms, relay_host_routing, c2c_monitor_ndjson. Evidence: B111 audit.